# 7. Constraints

The project is subject to the following constraints:

- Limited hackathon development time.
- Dataset is only available during the competition.
- Internet connectivity may be limited.
- Processing depends on available computing resources.

---

# 8. Risks

Potential risks include:

- Poor data quality
- Missing values
- Class imbalance
- Model overfitting
- Time limitations
- Merge conflicts in GitHub

Mitigation strategies include:

- Data preprocessing
- Cross-validation
- Clear team roles
- Frequent commits and Pull Requests
- Continuous testing

---

# 9. Acceptance Criteria

The project will be considered successful if it:

- Successfully loads and processes the dataset.
- Correctly predicts fraudulent transactions.
- Achieves acceptable evaluation metrics.
- Displays results in the dashboard.
- Provides useful business insights.
- Includes complete documentation.
- Demonstrates teamwork and proper GitHub workflow.

